 "summary": "The prior finding is fixed: the named deuteron channels now have `parity` and `PauliAllowed` lemmas (`tripletS1_parity`, `tripletD1_parity`, `pauliAllowed_tripletS1`, `pauliAllowed_tripletD1`), the last two at `@[simp high]` so they beat the general `pauliAllowed_iff_odd`. The rest of the surface is minimal and complete: bodies unexposed with `(rfl)`/`(Iff.rfl)` restatements, `*_def` plus characteristic iffs for every definition, `@[ext]` with no free data, and the general triangle-rule lemmas public in the upstream `PhyslibAlpha.Sl2` namespace rather than private.",
